{
  "_comment": "Experiments, sized so that the whole programme costs about USD 7 at list prices and can never exceed total_budget_usd: every run stops when the total spent (all experiments, plus the test calls of check_setup.py) would pass that amount, and when the experiment has used its own budget. Each block under 'calls' gives roles x models (optionally x reasoning efforts) and its sample: n_cal calibration loans (half defaulted, half repaid) and n_test randomly drawn test loans. Samples are nested, so a smaller sample is the first part of a larger one. Calls already in llm_outputs.csv are never repeated, so experiments share calls. 'teams' are the sets of agents on which the orchestration policies are evaluated; an agent is written role@model, or role@model#effort when the effort differs from the registry.",
